"The old willow is an ancient spirit tree, half awake, rooted on a vein of wood Qi."
"On a night of falling stars the willow called a soul across, and drew Alan's as he dozed."
"The willow grew Nala's body from its own Qi, in the shape of a woman who once tended it."
"That woman was a red-haired foreigner who lived at the bend long ago and died beneath it."
"Her bones lie among the willow's roots with a lacquered box of her things."
"Grown rather than born, Nala's body has meridians unusually clear and open to wood Qi."
"Near the willow Nala feels a faint calm, and a willow she tends slowly stirs to life."
